id: pm-qn9zxu
title: "GH-1229: preserve bounded HTTP process-tree cleanup when POSIX liveness returns EPERM"
description: macOS Node 24 nightly run 34457166668 throws kill EPERM in childTreeIsAlive while waiting for a nested HTTP server to exit. Zero-signal permission refusal is evidence of an existing process group; throwing immediately masks the expected discovery diagnostic and interrupts governed cleanup.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-10T10:21:49.623Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-10T11:05:19.540Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-10T10:35:37.937Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-10T10:35:37.937Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Real nested-server EPERM regression passes with original bounded cleanup and invalid-discovery diagnostics; port reuse remains required; unknown errors remain failures; exact coverage and hosted gates pass.
parent: pm-euqm7x
severity: medium
environment: macOS Node 24 and POSIX process groups
resolution: Zero-signal EPERM conservatively retains process-group liveness so the existing bounded shutdown continues; real nested-server fault injection verifies the diagnostic and port release.
expected_result: A transient liveness permission error cannot preempt governed shutdown or replace the discovery failure; existing readiness and shutdown bounds remain unchanged.
actual_result: 32 focused tests and 8682 tests in 660 files pass; exact statements/branches/functions/lines are 100 percent. The EPERM variant failed before the fix and passed with real signal delivery and port reuse after it. Hosted verification and the final non-overlapping static run remain subsequent delivery evidence.
regression: true
