comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-10T10:21:49.623Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete all-status searches for childTreeIsAlive EPERM and verify-published-release plus live open/in-progress lists found the completed timeout owner pm-euqm7x but no owner for this distinct liveness error. Reuse its lineage. Evidence https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1229 and run 34457166668 at 0a5e84b7bbf6fbe7ff22c12013f9f761d761a30c."
  "2026-09-10T10:25:24.341Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: the new parameterized nested-server fixture failed before the repair with injected kill EPERM masking Published HTTP discovery response was invalid (31 passed / 1 failed). Returning conservative liveness for zero-signal EPERM makes all 32 focused tests pass while retaining actual HTTP exchange, TERM/KILL delivery, bounded waits, and port reuse. The injected error is verified in stderr and does not replace actual process management. Test-only fallback cleanup occurs after assertions and only on failure. Unchanged-source nightly attempt 2 also passed, which demonstrates intermittency rather than constituting the repair."
  "2026-09-10T10:30:45.857Z","harness:codex","Verification note: the first overlapping static/coverage attempt passed correctness gates but SDK cold-import performance samples exceeded unchanged ceilings under concurrent full coverage. The source change only affects the release verifier; repeat performance-sensitive static checks after coverage finishes instead of weakening ceilings. Focused ESLint passes after preserving the original test failure through best-effort fallback cleanup."
  "2026-09-10T10:35:17.146Z","harness:codex","Full verification evidence: the isolated coverage command passed 660 test files and 8682 tests. Exact coverage remains statements 63924/63924; branches 48623/48623; functions 13290/13290; lines 61268/61268. The PM-linked focused command passes all 32 tests, and focused ESLint passes. No source coverage exclusions, timeout changes, or gate relaxations were introduced. The actual syscall-fault negative control failed before the conservative EPERM liveness repair and passed afterward; a final static run will execute without concurrent coverage load before push."
  "2026-09-10T10:44:18.532Z","harness:codex","Terminal local delivery evidence: the final non-overlapping pnpm quality:static run passed in full, including unchanged SDK cold-import and CLI transport ceilings, source/export/member docstrings, zero clones, contracts and generated surfaces, SDK/package/flag parity, refusal and token gates, tracker context, graph composition, and record integrity. Complete coverage passed 8682 tests at exact 100/100/100/100; final focused verifier rerun passed 32/32. No thresholds or assertions were relaxed. PR 1228 will carry this source and all closure evidence through exact-head hosted CI and review."
  "2026-09-10T11:05:19.540Z","harness:codex","Hosted delivery evidence: manual Nightly Validation run 34467694125 at exact PR head 4b35b1376934511ac56368139a4be8077504f74b passed all five jobs: Linux Node 22/24/25, macOS Node 24, and Windows Node 24. macOS build, typecheck, and actual tests passed, including native and injected-EPERM nested-server cleanup. All PR checks on that head also settled green. The full review identified a separate legacy-renderer correction under pm-5t33or; its new push will receive fresh PR checks. The nightly source fix itself is unchanged."
